course: dictionary
lesson: 258
title: Words that take turns
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: Alternate is a word with more than one meaning, so the words around it tell you which one you need. Read the clues first.
explain: To alternate means to change back and forth between two things, one after the other: red, blue, red, blue. «Brothers and sisters can share the front seat by taking turns, for example on alternate days.» On alternate days means one day yes, one day no.
explain: Alternate numbers are every other number: 1, 3, 5, 7, and so on. In a sentence, alternate often means every second one.
explain: In US English, alternate can also mean a spare choice, like an alternate route, or a person who can take someone's place. Ask yourself: is it about taking turns, or about a backup?
fact: Alternate can be a verb, an adjective, or a noun.
fact: «To alternate» means to change again and again between two things.
fact: «On alternate days» means every second day.
fact: «Alternate angles» are equal angles on opposite sides of a line crossing two parallel lines, used in maths.
fact: «Alternating current» (AC) is electricity that keeps changing direction, used in science.
exercise: «Brothers and sisters can share the front seat by taking turns, for example on alternate days.» What does on alternate days mean? | Every day, with no gaps | Only at weekends | Never at all | *One day yes, one day no
exercise: Which pattern alternates? | Red, red, red, red | Words in a long list | Only one colour all day | *Red, blue, red, blue
exercise: In maths, alternate numbers are 1, 3, 5, and so on. What is the next alternate number after 5? | 10 | *7 | 6 | 8
test: In a team, an alternate can take someone's place if they are hurt. What is an alternate? | A player who scores the most goals | A referee | A team captain | *A spare player who can take someone's place
test: «The sea floor has stripes of rock magnetised in alternate directions.» What does alternate mean here? | *Changing in turn, one direction then the other | Hidden under the water | Very strong | Matching
exam: Mia says alternate always means the same thing. Is she right? | Yes, it only means a sea floor | *No, it can mean changing back and forth, every second one, or a spare | Yes, it only ever means every second one | No, it always means very fast
